      {
        "id": "t18_title",
        "type": "flograph.util.note",
        "pos": [
          0,
          -320
        ],
        "params": {
          "text": "# Reading PDFs\n\n**Make Some PDFs** writes three documents to a folder, then the flow reads\nthem back two ways.\n\n**Read PDF (Folder)** turns the whole folder into one row per page, with a\n`file` column \u2014 so Group By, Filter Rows and every other transform work on a\nstack of documents the way they work on a CSV. Its second output lists the\ndocuments themselves: title, page count, and whether each one has a text\nlayer at all.\n\n**Read PDF** does the same for a single file, and **PDF Viewer** shows a page\nof it on the canvas and on the dashboard page.\n",
          "width": 480,
          "height": 360
        },
        "code": null,
        "label": null
      },
      {
        "id": "t18_payload_note",
        "type": "flograph.util.note",
        "pos": [
          600,
          900
        ],
        "params": {
          "text": "### Metadata, or metadata + bytes\n\nEvery PDF node asks how much of the document should travel down the wire.\n\n*Metadata only* \u2014 the default \u2014 puts the **path** on it. The document dict\nstays a few hundred bytes however big the file is.\n\n**Read PDF** here is set to *Metadata + bytes*, which adds the file itself\nand a `data_uri` for anything downstream that wants to embed it. Handy, and\nit costs the whole file in memory \u2014 which is why it is a choice and not a\ndefault.\n",
          "width": 420,
          "height": 260
        },
        "code": null,
        "label": null
      }
    ],
